To access the “user_agents” array in the JSON response, you can use the following code:


package main

import (
	“encoding/json”
	“fmt”
	“log”
	“net/http”
)

type Response struct {
	UserAgents []string json:"user_agents"
}

func getUserAgents() {
	url := “http://localhost:5000/api/get_ua”

	resp, err := http.Get(url)
	if err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}
	defer resp.Body.Close()

	var response Response

	err = json.NewDecoder(resp.Body).Decode(&response)
	if err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}

	for _, ua := range response.UserAgents {
		fmt.Println(ua)
	}
}

func main() {
	getUserAgents()
}



In this example, I introduced a new Response struct with a field UserAgents of type []string. The json:"user_agents" tag is used to match the field name in the JSON response.

The for loop then iterates over the UserAgents slice and prints each user agent.

